  "source_route": [
    "retain the exact compact witnesses of the existing original metric incidence proofs",
    "reuse original finite coefficient-module and faithful-prefix theorems in one quotient through actual inverse orthogonal pullbacks",
    "reuse finite-module separation, original fraction fields and denominator clearing to construct an original scalar-linear functional detecting one",
    "reuse finite residue-algebra nilpotence, multiplier ideals and ideal Artin-Rees for the actual adic filtrations",
    "derive original Taylor interpolation, exact original ideal-power kernels and remainders from independent polynomial and derivative specifications with opaque seals",
    "compare finite coefficient counts by the existing Chapter 1 dimension bounds and natural polynomial growth",
    "prove every nonempty arbitrary-ideal E_m has the original minimum-depth index, including zero and full indices",
    "reuse the original minimum-depth exclusion and finite compact-cover intersections; no closure under differences is assumed"
  ],
  "coverage_qualification": "This supplement closes the original real auxiliary sentence for arbitrary proper ideals, without a primeness, reducedness or geometric vanishing-ideal hypothesis. It does not assert the stronger complex auxiliary analogue. The previously released numbered complex Borel assertion remains complete. Explicit user omissions and the other completion-queue items remain.",
